Received arguments:
{
  "case_state": "Ticket NBL-017 (routine, kitchen extractor fan, Flat 1, 31 Juniper Mews). Landlord replied on 2026-09-15 that the fan's switch on the right-hand side of the hob needs switching on. This is a tenant self-fix. Now on hold waiting for the tenant to try the switch and confirm the result; review 2026-09-18.",
  "next_actions": [
    {
      "action": "Tell the tenant the landlord says the hob's right-hand switch may need turning on, and to reply if the fan still does not work so a contractor can be arranged.",
      "ledger_id": "A2",
      "type": "REPLY_TO_TENANT",
      "recipient": "Clara, tenant",
      "channel": "email"
    },
    {
      "action": "Hold the ticket for the tenant's reply; review on 2026-09-18 and chase the tenant if nothing has come back.",
      "ledger_id": "A3",
      "type": "WAIT",
      "recipient": "internal",
      "channel": "internal"
    },
    {
      "action": "If the fan still does not work after the switch is on, log the tenant's report and arrange a contractor under the landlord's decision and approval rules.",
      "type": "ASSIGN_PROVIDER",
      "recipient": "Northbridge operations, internal",
      "channel": "internal"
    }
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "Landlord's comment is a diagnosis, not a confirmed repair; it does not show the fan works.",
    "Switching the hob switch on does not confirm the fault is resolved.",
    "Not confirmed who pays; no contractor has been instructed or booked."
  ],
  "remaining_work": [
    "Tenant to try the switch and confirm whether the fan works (owner: tenant; review 2026-09-18).",
    "If not fixed: arrange a contractor; landlord's approval for a contractor is not yet on record.",
    "Tell the landlord the outcome, and close the ticket once confirmed."
  ],
  "missing_info": [
    "Whether the fan works after the switch is turned on.",
    "Landlord approval for a contractor, only needed if the tenant reports it still does not work."
  ],
  "outcome": "action_taken",
  "severity": "routine",
  "summary": "The landlord's reply (2026-09-15) says the extractor fan's switch on the right-hand side of the hob needs turning on, so the job was recorded as a tenant self-fix. The tenant was emailed with that instruction and asked to reply if the fan still does not work; the ticket is on hold until 2026-09-18.",
  "answers": [
    {
      "question": "Where does this case stand right now, and what is outstanding?",
      "answer": "Routine ticket NBL-017 is on hold, waiting for the tenant. The landlord's answer is that the hob's right-hand switch needs turning on. Still open: the tenant's confirmation that the fan works, and a contractor only if it does not."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the next action, who is it for, and through which channel?",
      "answer": "Email Clara (tenant) on the existing thread (event 007) with the switch instruction and the request to reply if it still fails (sent, MSG-101). Then review the hold on 2026-09-18."
    },
    {
      "question": "Does anything need a human decision, and why?",
      "answer": "No. The landlord's reply resolves the next step without spend or approval. A human is only needed if the tenant reports the fan still faulty and a contractor must be arranged beyond the landlord's stated decision."
    }
  ],
  "actions_claimed": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A1",
      "description": "Recorded landlord decision as tenant_self_fix on NBL-017 with landlord's quote."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A2",
      "description": "Sent email to tenant Clara (MSG-101) explaining the hob switch check."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A3",
      "description": "Put NBL-017 on hold, waiting for tenant, review 2026-09-18."
    }
  ],
  "failed_actions": [],
  "conflicts": [
    "The intake note says landlord approval is required first; the landlord has now replied, so approval is effectively answered as a self-fix rather than a contractor approval."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The tenant's email on the existing thread (event 007) is the right channel.",
    "The landlord's remark refers to the extractor fan, which is the ticket's subject."
  ],
  "boundaries_placeholder": "null"
}

